        "title": "Deviance and Social Control",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Deviance is **behavior that violates social norms and is subject to negative social sanctions**. It is not inherent to the act but to the social reaction — the same act can be deviant in one context and normal in another, by one social group and criminal by another. Social control includes all mechanisms — formal and informal — through which societies enforce conformity to norms."
